# Interface 16001 is GetBuildInfo() dumped from a running Forever 1.60.1
# client (.libraries/BlizzardInterfaceResources/README.md:7).
#
# IconAtlas is LFGF.ICON_ATLAS (core/main.lua), the window's portrait and the
# tab's icon. Category and IconAtlas are what the in-game AddOns list reads
# (Blizzard_AddOnList/AddonList.lua:390-395, :456); its search box matches
# Category, so "group finder" finds this addon.
#
# The three AddonCompartmentFunc lines put an entry in Blizzard's AddOns
# dropdown by the minimap, with IconAtlas beside the title. Blizzard calls the
# named GLOBALS, defined in core/minimap.lua
# (Blizzard_Minimap/Mainline/AddonCompartment.lua:102-149).
#
# LFGForeverDB holds every setting account-wide, the window position and size,
# the minimap button's angle, the saved Filters tab and My filters;
# LFGForeverCharDB holds the two settings saved per character, the Ask to Join
# and Invite whisper messages. Every key, its table and its default are listed
# in core/db.lua, the only file that touches the two tables.
#
# Version stays literal: releases are zipped by hand, so @project-version@
# would reach the load greeting unsubstituted. core/main.lua reads it.
#
# Files load in .toc order, each receiving (addonName, addonTable) as its `...`.
#
# Most of them publish functions on the private table and resolve each other at
# CALL time, so beyond the rules below the order is for readability. What a
# file reads at FILE scope must already be there, which gives five rules, all
# held by spec/LFGForever/window_spec.lua ("every file reads at load only what
# an earlier file defined"):
#   * core/locale.lua comes FIRST. It builds LFGF.L, every word the addon shows,
#     and loads a language pack into it if one is installed (a LoadOnDemand
#     addon marked "## X-LFGForever-LanguagePack: 1"). Every other file reads
#     LFGF.L at file scope, so nothing may run before it. No pack is named here:
#     locale.lua finds packs by that field. .claude/rules/language-packs.md
#   * core/db.lua comes SECOND: settings.lua reads its LFGF.SAVED_KEYS and
#     minimap.lua its LFGF.MINIMAP_DEFAULT_ANGLE at file scope.
#     .claude/rules/saved-variables-db.md
#   * core/main.lua comes THIRD. Five files read what it defines at file
#     scope: listpanel.lua (Readable, ClassIconAtlas, CreateRowActionButton,
#     ApplyActionLockTo, INVITE_ICON_ATLAS), filterpanel.lua (MY_FILTERS_MAX,
#     MY_FILTER_NAME_MAX_LETTERS), window.lua and blizzardtab.lua (TITLE) and
#     slash.lua (SLASH_COMMAND, TITLE).
#   * core/settings.xml comes after core/settings.lua, whose global mixin
#     (LFGForeverSettingsMessageRowMixin) its template names.
#   * core/filterpanel_shared.lua comes before core/filterpanel_miscellaneous.lua
#     and core/filterpanel.lua: both read its LFGF.FilterShared (the section
#     builders) at file scope. .claude/rules/filter-miscellaneous-section.md
# core/filterpanel_groupclasses.lua (the Groups section's class filter) sits
# beside the Miscellaneous section's file, before core/filterpanel.lua, which
# builds with it. .claude/rules/group-class-filter.md
# The panel factories come before core/window.lua, which builds with them, and
# core/blizzardtab.lua after it, since the tab opens that window.
core\locale.lua
core\db.lua
core\main.lua
core\relations.lua
core\talents.lua
core\settings.lua
core\settings.xml
core\listpanel.lua
core\whisperlog.lua
core\filterpanel_shared.lua
core\filterpanel_miscellaneous.lua
core\filterpanel_groupclasses.lua
core\filterpanel.lua
core\window.lua
core\blizzardtab.lua
core\minimap.lua
core\slash.lua
